comments[5]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-08T13:16:57.715Z","harness:claude-code","Duplicate check before filing: semantic search for 'DeepScan CodeFactor analyze direct pushes to main so direct commits carry exact analyzer evidence' returned only closed lineage (pm-39cqqx, pm-xcrlkl, pm-u1baah, pm-ji5c, pm-izid) and no open owner; pm-e70zh5 owns the rate, pm-44u3wt the cron window, pm-uenmu9 the same-day guard, pm-k9m6wc release immutability. Evidence: gh api commits/5da0aa6e5/status lists codecov/patch only and check-runs list nothing from an analyzer; commits/41ac9470f/status lists DeepScan, CodeRabbit, Hound and check-runs list codefactor-io/CodeFactor and semgrep. Scheduled run 34199116643 failed step 'Verify release analyzer provenance before build' with direct_main_policy refuse_without_exact_commit_analyzer_evidence."
  "2026-09-12T21:09:35.765Z","harness:codex","Live recurrence 2026-09-12: main CI run 34717518299 failed only Release analyzer readiness on 1e60ce072d9af3e819ed58bf0ec2100bf45dad40. This head arrived directly on main and lacks exact-commit or reviewed identical-tree analyzer evidence. The connected telemetry PR must restore analyzed provenance without weakening the gate. GitHub open PR and all three security alert inventories were empty."
  "2026-10-14T06:16:13.281Z","harness:codex","Chrome computer-use inspection of main2024387a346 confirms DeepScan GOOD with0 issues across1639 files and CodeFactor A with the same2 generated plugin duplication findings owned by pm-z3ez/GH1311/GH1312. DeepScan also exposes a separate legacy ESLint8.15.0 supplemental failure: No files matching the pattern dot were found. This is provider configuration evidence, separate from its successful zero-issue analysis and the repository ESLint10.12/zero-warning gate; no analyzer, gate or security setting was disabled. The new PR still needs its own exact-head analyzer receipt."
  "2026-10-17T09:30:36.190Z","harness:codex","Chrome refresh October 17: DeepScan main eeeaf3ececc4fc18c6c41cf3c4a5d3218e92a0aa reports GOOD and zero native issues. Supplemental ESLint remains its embedded 8.15.0 failure: No files matching the pattern dot were found. CodeFactor main is A with the same two generated plugin/template duplication groups, owned by pm-z3ez and GitHub 1311/1312. Preserve this separate provider limitation and the repository ESLint 10 gate; no provider settings or required analyzer thresholds were disabled."
  "2026-10-17T14:31:36.735Z","harness:codex","PR1490 operational observation: exact source1d974eaa2 passed every GitHub Actions workflow, CodeFactor and exact100/100/100/100 coverage with zero skipped coverage entries. Native DeepScan remains pending Analyzing with no result URL after more than30minutes. Chrome shows the official service status Operational and no completed current-head result. The repository webhook is active; the synchronize delivery returned HTTP200, and one existing-delivery retry was acceptedHTTP202. No cause is confirmed, and its relationship to the older provenance/embedded-ESLint issue is unknown. Record this evidence and request a fresh automatic analysis with the metadata head; keep the required analyzer gate intact. Six actionable inline review findings are resolved; remaining requested reviews report provider quota or plan limits."
